{
  "name": "AI Analysis App — History Endpoint v1",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI Analysis App — GET /history Endpoint\n\n### Setup Checklist\n1. Replace `YOUR_SUPABASE_URL` with your Supabase project URL\n2. Replace `YOUR_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` with your Supabase anon/public key\n3. Make sure you've run the SQL from Backend v1 (the `analyses` table + RLS policy)\n\n### What Your Frontend Sends\n```json\nPOST /webhook/ai-history\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"token\": \"<supabase_session_jwt>\",\n  \"limit\": 20,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n```\n`limit` and `offset` are optional — default to 20 and 0.\n\n### Response Your Frontend Receives\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"data\": [\n    { \"id\": \"uuid\", \"created_at\": \"...\", \"result\": {...}, \"input_metadata\": {...} },\n    ...\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Notes\n- Results are scoped to the authenticated user via Supabase RLS (auth.uid() = user_id)\n- Sorted newest first (order=created_at.desc)\n- Extend with `?select=id,created_at` to return only specific fields",
        "height": 680,
        "width": 1340,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [-120, -380],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "h1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
      "name": "Setup Guide"
    },
